From: Harsh Menon <harmenon@cv350-zts-gtu-g31-18.prov.gtu.zts.cpe.ice.amd.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Mar 2026 22:56:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20gfx1250=20B0=E2=86=92A0=20in-place=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?binary=20patches=20for=20three=20A0=20hardware=20bugs?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three B0-emitted instructions cause hardware bugs on A0 silicon:
- CLUSTER_LOAD multicast lockup (DEGFXMI400-12773): rewrite to GLOBAL_LOAD
- DS 2-address payload alignment (DEGFXMI400-12320): rewrite to single-address
- s_clause cross-scope mismatch (SWDEV-546277): replace with s_nop

All patches are same-size opcode rewrites — no trampolines or LLVM MC needed.
The B0→A0 path short-circuits in RetargetCodeObject before LLVM init when
src==tgt==gfx1250. Also adds gfx1250/gfx1251 to gfx_mach_map, a C-linkage
wrapper, CLI retarget tool, standalone unit tests (5/5 passing), and a Triton
integration test script.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
