From 80c5e8fd82e3f7619ef8265ecd3a6d01f65cc5eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsh Menon <harmenon@cv350-zts-gtu-g31-18.prov.gtu.zts.cpe.ice.amd.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 02:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20ELF=20growth=20for=20tensor=5Fload=5F?=
 =?UTF-8?q?to=5Flds=20B0=E2=86=92A0=20patches=20and=20integration=20tests?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tensor_load_to_lds patches were silently skipped when kernels had no NOP
sled space after s_endpgm (all 4 real Triton kernels hit this). Now falls
back to appending trampolines beyond .text via ELF growth, fixing up all
section/program headers. Also fixes a bug where the section header fixup
loop broke early, skipping offset updates for sections after .text.

Adds rocr_hotswap_gfx1250_b0_to_a0_grow() C API that returns a grown
buffer, and 7 integration tests on real Triton .hsaco kernels verifying
patch counts, s_pack_hh_b32_b16 placement, ELF validity, idempotency,
and non-target instruction preservation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
