From 5ef42bd34172f9539ecaf6668ded61dd0c43bad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsh Menon <harmenon@cv350-zts-gtu-g31-18.prov.gtu.zts.cpe.ice.amd.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 03:11:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Fix s_branch encoding for GFX12: use opcode 0x20 (0xBFA0)
 not 0x02 (0xBF82)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GFX12 renumbered SOPP opcodes: s_branch moved from opcode 0x02 to 0x20.
The old encoding 0xBF820000 decodes as s_sethalt on GFX12, which would
halt the GPU instead of branching to/from trampolines.

EncodeSBranch now takes a gfx12 flag to select the correct opcode.
All B0→A0 (gfx1250) call sites pass gfx12=true. The GFX9 retarget path
and unit tests continue using the default (gfx12=false).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
