From 13748f2fdcc7e77010c9d2489ffdebd76f226d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsh Menon <harmenon@cv350-zts-gtu-g31-18.prov.gtu.zts.cpe.ice.amd.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 18:40:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Fix WMMA hazard to WAR model and add synthetic hazard
 insertion tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The WMMA co-execution hazard is WAR (Write-After-Read), not RAW:
subsequent VALU instructions that write (clobber) WMMA input operands
while the WMMA is still co-executing create the hazard. Updated
CheckVgprOverlap to check VALU dest against all WMMA operands (D/C
accumulator, A, B matrices — since D is tied to C in the MCInst).

Also fixes:
- v_nop encoding: use LLVM MC assembly (0x7E000000) not hardcoded 0x00
- ClassifyWmmaNops: match LLVM's _fp8/_bf8 mnemonics (not just _f8)

Added 13 synthetic WMMA hazard tests:
- F8x64/F8x128/F8F6F4 immediate hazard (WAR on C-matrix)
- Partial NOPs, sufficient NOPs (no hazard)
- F16/IU8 no-delta (no hazard for equal/reversed timing)
- Non-overlapping VALU safe slots, SALU not counted
- Read-only D output (no WAR), clobber A-matrix (WAR)
- No overlap (no hazard), multiple hazards

22 tests pass (4 kernel + 3 structural + 2 classification + 13 synthetic).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
